menu "SIOT Provisioning (autoconnect POC)"

    config SIOT_FACTORY_DEV_ID
        string "Factory device id (sticker) -- POC fallback only"
        default "dev-001"
        help
            pocs/POC-BRIEF.md section 4.1 says the factory NVS namespace
            "siot_fact" (id, pop) is written by tools/make_sticker.py and
            must never be generated at runtime. That tool does not exist in
            this repo yet, so this value is used ONLY when "siot_fact" is
            empty in NVS, purely to unblock this POC on a bare devkit.
            Remove once the factory partition flow (make_sticker.py +
            nvs_partition_gen) exists.

    config SIOT_FACTORY_POP
        string "Factory POP secret (sticker) -- POC fallback only"
        default "abc123POP0000"
        help
            See SIOT_FACTORY_DEV_ID. WPA2 requires 8+ characters; the
            blueprint specifies 16+ for the real sticker POP.

    config SIOT_DEV_MODEL
        string "Device model string"
        default "SIOT-SENSOR-01"
        help
            pocs/APP-BRIEF.md section 5 step 2: the board's sticker model
            must start with "SIOT-BOARD" so the app's wizard can detect it
            automatically -- set this to e.g. "SIOT-BOARD-01" when building
            for the board role below.

    choice SIOT_ROLE
        prompt "Unit role"
        default SIOT_ROLE_NODE
        help
            POST /enroll (pocs/POC-BRIEF.md section 5) is only served when
            this is the board.

        config SIOT_ROLE_NODE
            bool "node (AC device / battery detector)"
        config SIOT_ROLE_BOARD
            bool "board (raises the installation network; never a mesh node)"
    endchoice

endmenu
